ent-BaseFoundationPDA = PDA
    .desc = Universal baseline corporate PDA: an autonomous terminal for accounting, communication, and information access. Reliable and simple to use, with a basic module set and upgrade capability.
ent-ScpEngineeringPDA = engineering PDA
    .desc = Modified PDA with a suite of engineering utilities: equipment diagnostics, geolocation, and network zone debugging. Ideal for repair, system configuration, and emergency recovery.
ent-ScpMedicalPDA = medical PDA
    .desc = Medical PDA with an anatomy database, pharmacology, and first-aid protocols. Includes tools for monitoring vitals and stabilization recommendations for patients.
ent-ScpSecurityPDA = security PDA
    .desc = Security service PDA with access to clearance logs, wanted personnel lists, and response protocols. Equipped with a reinforced chassis and tougher display.
ent-ScpResearchPDA = research PDA
    .desc = Research PDA with an extensive scientific database, experiment protocols, and a Foundation library. Supports storing experimental records.
ent-ScpServicePDA = service PDA
    .desc = Service PDA for support staff. It streamlines work coordination and documentation of completed tasks.
ent-ScpLogisticsPDA = logistics PDA
    .desc = Logistics PDA with warehouse management, delivery routes, and cargo accounting modules. Allows checking waybills and optimizing supply documentation.
ent-FacilityDirectorPDA = facility director's PDA
    .desc = Facility director's personal PDA with elevated access rights, encrypted email, and classified archives. Used for decision-making and management of key site resources.
ent-PersonnelManagerPDA = personnel manager PDA
    .desc = Personnel manager PDA includes staff files, shift schedules, intake and discharge protocols, and personnel evaluation tools. Ensures compliance with personnel procedures and data confidentiality.
ent-ChiefEngineerPDA = chief engineer's PDA
    .desc = Chief engineer's PDA with infrastructure system map, repair log, and preventive maintenance plan. Intended for strategic oversight of technical condition and coordination of technician teams.
ent-ScpQuartermasterPDA = quartermaster PDA
    .desc = Quartermaster PDA for managing stock flows, resource distribution, and coordinating supplies between departments. Includes inventory reports.
ent-ChiefMedicalOfficerPDA = chief medical officer's PDA
    .desc = Chief medical officer's PDA with expanded clinical references, priority patient list, medical staff schedules, and departmental procedure protocols. Serves for rapid management of medical operations.
ent-ResearchDirectorPDA = research director PDA
    .desc = Research director PDA combines strategic research plans, access to restricted publications, project budgets, and results reports. A tool for managing scientific activity and distributing research tasks.
ent-SecurityCommanderPDA = security commander PDA
    .desc = Security commander PDA with full access to monitoring systems, guard deployments, and emergency protocols. Allows issuing assignments, analyzing threats, and giving field orders.
ent-MobileTaskForcePDA = mobile task force PDA
    .desc = Field PDA for mobile task force teams: rapid access to maps, target data, orders, and action logs. Optimized for work in autonomous and extreme conditions.
ent-ChaosInsurgencyPDA = Chaos Insurgency operative PDA
    .desc = Field PDA for Chaos Insurgency operatives: quick access to maps, target data, orders, and an action log. Optimized for use in autonomous and extreme conditions.
ent-RegionalAdministrationPDA = Regional Administration PDA
    .desc = High-level administrative PDA with limited but critical access to directives, policy drafts, and secure communication channels. Intended for managing organizational decisions and leadership coordination.
ent-ScpAdminPDA = SCP admin PDA
    .suffix = Admin
    .desc = If you find this PDA, report it to the nearest AHelp post immediately and return it to Administration.
